## Inline requirements (cite the specific paragraph next to the decision it justifies)

Pull the concrete, checkable numbers out into their own subsections — minimum room areas,
corridor widths, fire-zone limits, whatever this typology's code actually constrains. Each
number gets its own `§` citation, e.g.:

> Minimum bedroom area: **X m²** (WT § NNN ust. N pkt N).

Numbers that later become a validator rule (`validators/_standards/<typology>-baseline.yaml`)
should be flagged as such here, so the rule's own `description` can point back to this file.

## Sourcing note

Record HOW each citation was obtained: a real reference drawing's own annotations, an existing
project document already in this repo, or web research against the primary source (not a
secondary summary). Never leave a citation that was invented from general recollection without
verifying the actual text.
